####
# Build-context allow-list.
#
# The repository carries a gigabyte of desktop-agent build trees, an installed
# node_modules, and every document the product has ever been tested with. None
# of it is read by `npm run build`, and sending it to the daemon costs more than
# the build itself. So: exclude everything, then add back the files the client
# and server builds actually open.
#
# A new top-level input to the build needs a line here as well as a COPY in the
# Dockerfile, or the COPY fails with "file not found" — a loud failure, which is
# the point of the allow-list over a deny-list.
####

*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!vite.config.ts
!tailwind.config.ts
!postcss.config.js
!client
!server
!shared
!script

# `script/` builds; `scripts/` is what the second build output is built from —
# `scripts/migrate.ts` becomes dist/migrate.mjs (#35). The two names are one
# letter apart and neither is optional. The whole directory is allowed through
# because it is small and this list is per top-level input; the Dockerfile then
# copies only `migrate.ts` and `lib/`, so the release and upload scripts never
# reach a layer.
!scripts

# Read at runtime rather than build time: the migration runner in the image
# resolves the journal beside itself, so `migrations/` is copied into the final
# stage and never touched by the build.
!migrations

# The directories above bring anything nested inside them; these never belong in
# an image regardless of where they turn up.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
